  "summary": "I wrote `src/main.ts`, and `typecheck` passes. I did not run `vite build` or open the page in a browser, so how it looks and whether `__EVAL_READY__` gets set are untested.\n\n- **Crystals:** There are seven, each built with `geometry.define` as a 5–7-sided prism with a pointed top. Heights, radii and tilts all differ. Each face has its own vertices, a flat normal and its own colour. Each crystal is a separate node.\n- **Rotation:** Every frame the crystals are moved around the cluster axis, and each one also turns on its own Y axis. They stand on a stacked cylinder pedestal over a ground disc.\n- **Sparks:** Six additive `effects.particles` emitters sit in a ring around the cluster. I set gravity to 0 and assumed the particles drift upward by default, as the flame emitters in the docs do. I haven't confirmed that.\n- **Look:** The background is near-black. Cyan and magenta directional rim lights come from behind, with a dim cool key light, a violet point glow, and bloom.\n- **Animation and ready flag:** The cluster rotation changes every frame, and the particles move as well. `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set one animation frame after `app.ready()` resolves.\n\nI guessed the pedestal and ground cylinder sizes, assuming `size` is `[diameter, height, diameter]`. If it means something else, they will look the wrong size.\n\n",
